              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tankee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a simple and quick receipe. I usually use about 1/4 cup of mustard and 1/4 cup of ketchup. It gives it a thicker sauce. I sprinkle with brown sugar a teasppon of brown sugar, half a teaspoon on garlic powder and half a teasppon of salt and black pepper after it is done to give that final seasoning."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JacobKeys"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I really love this recipe. I'd recommend pan-frying the wings in a pre-heated pan with a tablespoon each of olive oil and unsalted butter. Do the meaty side first for 10 minutes, covered, then when you flip the wings, add 1/4 a cup of water to the sauce that'll be forming in the pan, and fry the wings for another 5 minutes.\nWhen they're done, the wings will be incredibly juicy and tender, and covered in a sticky, finger-licking good sauce.\nAlso, try serving these with a nice broccoli salad on the side!",
            "datePublished": "2020-11-13T22:55:50.710Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
